  "formatVersion": 1,
  "name": "a-failed-bind-is-retried-with-backoff",
  "description": "A bind that fails stops the listener and, for up to three failures since the last bind that became ready, schedules a retry after 2, 4 and 6 seconds. Each retry clears the problem while it binds. A ready bind resets the count; an explicit start does not, and invalidates a pending retry. A waiting bind shows its problem but is left to the platform's own retries.",
  "reason": "Port contention arrives as a failed bind; without a retry one transient clash would leave the listener down for the session (HK-292).",
  "source": "rust/powerup-core/src/protocol/listener.rs, ported from Sources/PowerUp/RemoteListener.swift at 4c7abe6:66-73, 154-196 (handleListenerState), 198-203 (describe)",
  "verifiedBy": "DESIGN.md v1.4, v1.7, v2.15; docs/protocol.md spec v0. Rust: rust/powerup-core/tests/listener.rs listener_scenarios plays every step through protocol::listener::Listener. Swift: Tests/PowerUpTests/ListenerScenarioTests.swift testEveryListenerScenario plays every step through the bridge (CoreBridge.ListenerPolicy), and ProtocolServerTests drives the same policy over a real loopback socket.",
  "steps": [
